    "kind": "bench",
    "repro": "node --experimental-transform-types plugins/marks/benches/bigwigPaths.bench.ts --file=HG008_log2ratio.500bp.bw --refName=chr1 --screenPx=400000 --zooms=600,2500 --rounds=15 --json, and again with --index",
    "notes": "On ada (load average 12-17 over the run), over the 54 MB 500 bp-bin HG008 log2 ratio BigWig, one 400,000 px screen of chr1 at 600 and 2500 bp/px, bbi's block cache warm. Wiggle is getFeatureArraysMulti and processFeaturesFromArrays; table is getFeatureTable and encodeFeatures over the bar's lanes, with the index lane (--index, what a bar asked for before ADR-196) or without it. The build is what the hover's structure costs once per region: the Flatbush hitIndexOf in the worker on every fetch, or rowSpanIndex on the main thread at the first hover. The hover is the mean of 5000 findMarkHit calls at random points over the screen, 971 and 1091 of them hits, which answered identically both ways before any time was taken. MIN across rounds."
